Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:19:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] The Table, core (U17): tonight, a page per devotion,
 table mode

/family opens on a PageHead and Tonight at the table (title, passage, ten minutes, Start into table mode), then this week's catechism question and the season's daily sets, then the library, catechism, reading plans and tools. The four empty essay rows and the posts.listPublished download that fed them are gone.

/family/tonight resolves tonight's devotion from the static year map and the reader's own calendar and replaces itself with that devotion's page (carrying ?mode=table). /family/devotions/:id gives each of the 72 weekly devotions (frozen ids) and each day of the Thanksgiving, Advent and Holy Week sets its own page, with Send, Save and Print and a print stylesheet that fits every devotion on one Letter or A4 page. The accordion is retired; /family/devotions is now a list of doors with the tab in the URL.

Table mode (?mode=table): one part per screen on the Stepper (Read, Talk, Ask, Do, Remember, Pray), large type, Listen on the passage, the step in the URL, the screen kept awake (Screen Wake Lock), ending on We did this tonight, which records the date in livewell-progress-family-v1 and sends family_devotion_complete (id and mode only). Position: a quiet Position primitive, Week N of the year, Last time.

Data: client/public/family/index.json from scripts/build-family-index.mjs (one row per devotion page, Study Bible hrefs from the shared parser, the catechism's questions), --check in CI. Route checklist 9.3: App.tsx, the manifest, LIBRARY_SOURCES, the sitemap, paramSources, llms.txt; validate-family PAGES updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

